From f30201de0fe2400f769b05a17715d9d4771bcfc7 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Joseph Telaak <joseph@telaak.dev>
Date: Thu, 12 Nov 2026 17:40:40 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 11/21] meson, sgx/common: add the sgx gallium driver option
 and the per-core table

Add 'sgx' to -Dgallium-drivers (with_gallium_sgx) and enter src/sgx for it,
as -Dtools=sgx already does.

src/sgx/common holds one entry per SGX core: what the kernel doesn't
report through DRM_POWERVR_SGX_DEV_QUERY (the ISA variant, sampler count,
texture size, render-target limits on the services path). The SGX545 is
the only entry; a core without one is not driven.

Nothing builds the driver yet; the following commits add it piece by
piece.

Assisted-by: LLM
